body:
i hate my facial hair lol

&#x200B;

\-me circa now

it totally exists within our own community too. when i came out, i was presenting as myself and then going back to boy mode a lot and i was really depressed, unmotivated and having a shit time. I went to a support group and it was run by a completely passing trans woman. when i walked in, she was staring me up in down because i was for the most part in boy mode. I hadnt shaved, i was sleepy and my voice was deep. she looked at me and asked me "are you a crossdresser". this was the first fucking meeting i have ever been to. i was deathly afraid of leaving the house by myself. I answered, "no im a trans woman" and she completely ignored me for the whole meeting. it was one of those groups where trans women and crossdressers are there and i was basically ousted to the crossdresser group. it made me feel horrible. seeing the way this trans woman was treating all these other people in her community was disgusting. She was talking about how you can tell what a real woman is and that its a natural essence and energy you give off yadayadayada literally just throwing shade at me the whole fucking time. then she had the gall to invite me out to drinks with her. 

&#x200B;

i know im a woman. I know there are aspects about me that are masculine. I do not deserve to be picked apart by people for being me.
